THE RESULT the guess is about: UDP loss_frac=0.510489 and l1_drops=911591 while tcp_goodput_bps=0.
THE GUESS of why it came out so: Loss-based Cubic backs off under this high loss, whereas BBR's bandwidth/delay estimation may keep inflight and deliver more.
THE HYPOTHESIS H7: With l1.queue.length=4 fixed, TcpBbr gives tcp_goodput_bps more than 1 Mbps above TcpCubic.
DECISION RULE: tcp_goodput_bps@bbr_q4 - tcp_goodput_bps@cubic_q4 > 1000000
